# SQLBolt Day 4 - Filtering & Sorting
-- Date : 2/7/2026

## Topics Covered
- DISTINCT
- ORDER BY
- ASC
- DESC
- LIMIT
- OFFSET

## Key Notes

### DISTINCT
Removes duplicate values from the result.

### ORDER BY
Sorts the result set.

- ASC → Ascending order (Default)
- DESC → Descending order

### LIMIT
Returns only the specified number of rows.

### OFFSET
Skips a specified number of rows before returning results.

## Example

```sql
SELECT DISTINCT director
FROM movies
ORDER BY director ASC;
```

```sql
SELECT title, year
FROM movies
ORDER BY year DESC
LIMIT 4;
```

```sql
SELECT title
FROM movies
ORDER BY title ASC
LIMIT 5 OFFSET 5;
```

